  `gather_into(p, t, ..)` fills output pixel q from source `t(q)`, so the
  warped frame is the source warped by t^-1. The expected increment is
  therefore 1/s - 1, built with the EXACT inverse: at s = 1.02 the
  difference between -(s-1) and 1/s-1 is 0.83 plane px, which is larger
  than the whole effect being measured.

  Recovered gain = (measured increment) / (1/s - 1). Unity means the
  estimator's scale response is undistorted by the defocus gap.

